st rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Nebraska's R+10 partisan lean makes it one of the more Republican states in presidential voting, and that fundamentals-based advantage drives this forecast. No statewide polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market pricing are available for the presidential race itself; recent market and media attention has centered on Nebraska's Senate contest and the competitive 2nd Congressional District 'blue dot' rather than the statewide outcome.\n\nWith no incumbent president on the ballot and no candidate-specific polling or fundraising data, uncertainty is elevated and the expected margin carries an unusually wide band. The forecast expects the Republican nominee to carry the statewide vote by a double-digit margin, with the Democratic path requiring an unusually strong national environment. Debates over how Nebraska awards its electoral votes do not change the statewide picture, where the Republican advantage remains substantial.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1258, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1632, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1797, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1802, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1712, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1741, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1653, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1776, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1721, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -10.0}]}